  "weepingLamp": {
    "title": "Weeping Lamp",
    "description": "A lampshade carefully put together using wax holds then shards of pink gold ruby glass resembling scars. When the lamp is on, the bulb melts the wax, and those scars are slowly shed. This piece evokes the melancholy and beauty of healing and change of shedding the scars that were used to help us cope but ultimately dim our inner light. This process is a constant cycle of transmutation within the mind. This piece is an installation video paired with the *Guarding Rug* provides sound for the video that is meant for the viewer to piece together.",
    "materials": "Found Rug, Found Table, Found Lamp, Glass, Wax, Incandescent bulb, Paint, and Gold Leaf",
    "year": "2025",
