  "familyRepast": {
    "title": "Family Repast",
    "description": "The dinner table is a site for communicating through acts of care that transcends language and cultural barriers. The video is of various hands from two different families coming together to share a meal and become one family through marriage. The transparent glass of the objects from the video placed over it is a means of viewing. The video is not always clear, and the viewer is not always sure what is going on. Except for small moments of clarity that intentionally show that act of this family feeding one another. This is meant to portray the feeling one has of uncertainty and lack of knowledge when there are cultural and language barriers, yet the act of care and food is universal.",
    "materials": "Video, iPad, Glass, and Table",
    "year": "2024",
