  "theWindow": {
    "title": "The Window",
    "description": "This piece explores how one can never truly understand themselves. Using iridescence (the physical manifestation of light interference) as a metaphor for the various interferences in life that make it impossible to see your own reflection clearly. From afar the decadently decorated frame is reminiscent of a mirror, but once one gets up close, you realize that the glass has a mark representative of traditional window making. This object is meant to act as the portal into the mind we cannot see or reach.",
    "materials": "Vinyl, Wood, and Glass",
    "size": "15\" x 12\"",
    "year": "2024",
