  "aWalkThroughMyRoseWindow": {
    "title": "A Walk Through My Rose Window",
    "description": "This piece is meant to draw comparison to the use of light in spaces and how it can reflect the people who use it. It is meant to draw attention to the differing aspects of light in a sacred space and not directly decide which is better, but rather propose a new way of acknowledging light in a space. The piece references a rose window through its circular shape, the placement of the glass, and use of light. It differs because it is on the floor and constantly changing. It is accessible to any viewer in the same way that lighting a candle in a church can be. It allows viewers to be immersed within the piece that fills the space instead of a rose window that reveals light from above. It was installed in a space where viewers could walk through the installation and light candles themselves.",
    "materials": "Blown Stressed Glass, Candle, Fire, Liquid Gold Leaf",
    "year": "2023",
